// ===================================================================
// 🚀 HOW TO TEST BACKEND IN CONVEX DASHBOARD
// ===================================================================
//
// Before building the frontend, test these mutations work:
//
// 1. Go to Convex dashboard (https://dashboard.convex.dev)
// 2. Select your deployment
// 3. Go to "Functions" tab
//
// TEST SEQUENCE:
// ==============
//
// Step 1: Generate Upload URL
// Function: documents:generateUploadUrl
// Args: {} (no arguments)
// Result: You should get a URL like "https://storage.convex.cloud/..."
//
// Step 2: Upload File (using curl or browser)
// curl -X POST \
//   "[paste the URL from step 1]" \
//   -H "Content-Type: text/plain" \
//   --data-binary "@test.txt"
// Result: {"storageId": "kg2abcd1234..."}
//
// Step 3: Create Document
// Function: documents:createFromFile
// Args: {
//   "fileId": "kg2abcd1234..." (paste storageId from step 2),
//   "title": "Test Document",
//   "type": "text"
// }
// Result: Document ID like "kg2xyz789..."
//
// Step 4: Watch Processing
// Function: documents:getById (if you have it)
// Args: { "id": "kg2xyz789..." }
// Check: status should change from "processing" → "ready"
// Check: content should have extracted text
//
// Step 5: Verify Search
// Function: documents:list (or search if you have it)
// Check: Document appears in list
// Check: contentPlain field is populated
//
// ===================================================================